{
  "duration": 71.72,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.319,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.039,
      "end": 3.159,
      "text": "It's time to solve"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.579,
      "end": 4.48,
      "text": "one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.199,
      "end": 8.679,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, we have a train of length two hundred forty meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.319,
      "end": 11.0,
      "text": "It crosses a platform of length"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.5,
      "end": 13.699,
      "text": "two hundred sixty meter in twenty-five seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.199,
      "end": 17.779,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the speed of the train in kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.18,
      "end": 19.479,
      "text": "Now, the important point here is,"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.939,
      "end": 21.259,
      "text": "crosses a platform."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.639,
      "end": 22.859,
      "text": "What does this actually mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.199,
      "end": 28.519,
      "text": "When a train completely crosses a platform, it has to cover its own length as well as the length of the platform."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.979,
      "end": 30.42,
      "text": "So the total distance covered will be"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.879,
      "end": 33.479,
      "text": "train length plus platform length."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.899,
      "end": 37.419,
      "text": "That is two hundred forty plus two hundred sixty equals five hundred meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.799,
      "end": 38.139,
      "text": "Got it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.639,
      "end": 39.019,
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.639,
      "end": 41.979,
      "text": "Now that we have the total distance, we can find the speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.299,
      "end": 45.559,
      "text": "We know speed equals distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.039,
      "end": 54.079,
      "text": "Putting the values, speed equals five hundred divided by twenty-five. After solving this, we get speed equals twenty meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.479,
      "end": 61.219,
      "text": "Now, the question is asking for the answer in kilometers per hour, so we convert it using twenty times eighteen by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.599,
      "end": 64.199,
      "text": "That gives us seventy-two kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.959,
      "end": 65.36,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.76,
      "end": 71.72,
      "text": "the speed of the train is seventy-two kilometer per hour. So the correct option is option C."
    }
  ],
